# A shell script or a python module checked out with CRLF does not run: the
# kernel reads \r as part of the interpreter path. Windows needs these LF even
# in a Windows checkout, so they are pinned rather than left to core.autocrlf.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary, so git neither converts them nor tries to diff them.
*.dic binary
*.onnx binary
*.zip binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ogg binary
